      <p>This is a translation for customers. The German privacy notice is the binding version.</p>
      <h2>1. Controller</h2>
      <p>Paul Grossfeld<br>Konradstraße 8<br>48145 Münster<br>Germany<br>Phone: <a href="tel:+491771475356">+49 177 1475356</a><br>Email: <a href="mailto:Grossfeld.paul@gmail.com">Grossfeld.paul@gmail.com</a></p>
      <p>No data protection officer has been appointed. This shop is not required to appoint one.</p>
      <h2>2. Why we process data</h2>
      <p>We process personal data to fulfil orders, run the shop, answer enquiries and — only if you consent — send the newsletter.</p>
      <h2>3. Orders</h2>
      <p>When you order, we process the data needed for the contract and delivery: name, shipping and billing address, email, phone number if provided, items ordered, order value and a payment reference.</p>
      <p>The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR. We keep invoice and accounting records for the statutory retention period, usually eight years (section 147 of the German Fiscal Code). After that we delete or restrict them.</p>
      <p>Checkout and hosting run on Shopify. Shopify processes the data on our behalf where it acts as a processor. Shopify’s privacy notice: <a href="https://www.shopify.com/legal/privacy">shopify.com/legal/privacy</a>.</p>
      <h2>4. Payment</h2>
      <p>Payment data is processed by the provider you choose at checkout, in particular PayPal, Klarna and Shopify Payments (card, Shop Pay), under their own responsibility. We do not receive the full card number. Sharing the order data needed for payment is based on Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR.</p>
      <h2>5. Contact form</h2>
      <p>If you write to us through the form, we process your name, email and message to answer you. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR if it relates to an order or contract, otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. We delete the enquiry once the matter is closed and no retention duty applies.</p>
      <h2>6. Newsletter</h2>
      <p>If you sign up for the newsletter, we store your email address to send you news about Capshot. Where a confirmation email is set up, we store the signup only after double opt-in. The legal basis is your consent, Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR. You can withdraw it at any time, for example via the unsubscribe link. Processing before withdrawal remains lawful.</p>
      <h2>7. Server logs and cookies</h2>
      <p>When you open the shop, Shopify processes the technical connection data needed to run it, such as IP address, date, time, page requested and browser type. This is for operation, security and troubleshooting. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.</p>
      <p>Cookies and similar storage that are required for the cart, checkout and displaying the shop are set under section 25(2) TDDDG. We set optional analytics or marketing cookies only if you have consented (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR, section 25(1) TDDDG).</p>
      <h2>8. Recipients and countries outside the EEA</h2>
      <p>Recipients are Shopify as host and checkout, the payment providers named above and, where used, a carrier for delivery. We do not pass data to third parties for their own advertising.</p>
      <p>Shopify and payment providers may also process data outside the European Economic Area. Where there is no adequacy decision, they rely on standard contractual clauses or a comparable safeguard under Art. 46 GDPR.</p>
      <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, data portability and to object to processing based on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. You can withdraw consent at any time with effect for the future.</p>
      <p>You may lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority, in particular in the member state of your residence or of the alleged infringement. Our authority is the State Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information of North Rhine-Westphalia (LDI NRW).</p>
      <p>Order data is required to perform the contract. Without it we cannot deliver. You do not have to join the newsletter.</p>
      <p>We do not make automated decisions within the meaning of Art. 22 GDPR that produce a legal effect concerning you. Fraud checks by payment providers remain their own processing.</p>
