      <p>We deliver within Germany to the address you provide. Delivery takes 2 to 5 business days after the contract is formed, while the item is in stock. If the product page states a different time when you order, that time applies.</p>
      <h2>5. Retention of title</h2>
      <p>The goods remain our property until paid in full.</p>
      <h2>6. Withdrawal</h2>
      <p>Consumers have the statutory right of withdrawal. The instructions and the model withdrawal form are on the <a href="{{ pages.widerruf.url | default: '/pages/widerruf' }}">withdrawal</a> page.</p>
      <h2>7. Defects</h2>
      <p>Statutory defect rights apply. Claims for defects in new goods expire two years after delivery.</p>
      <h2>8. Liability</h2>
      <p>We are liable without limit for intent and gross negligence, for injury to life, body or health, under the German Product Liability Act, and where we have given a guarantee.</p>
      <p>For slight negligence we are liable only for breach of an essential contractual duty whose fulfilment makes proper performance of the contract possible and on which you regularly rely. Liability is then limited to the foreseeable damage typical for this kind of contract.</p>
      <h2>9. Age</h2>
      <p>Sale to persons aged 18 and over only.</p>
      <h2>10. Dispute resolution and governing law</h2>
      <p>We are neither willing nor obliged to take part in dispute resolution before a consumer arbitration board.</p>
      <p>The law of the Federal Republic of Germany applies, excluding the UN Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods. For consumers, this choice of law applies only so far as it does not deprive them of the protection of mandatory rules of the law of the country where they habitually reside.</p>
      <p>We do not agree an exclusive place of jurisdiction against consumers. Statutory venues remain in place.</p>
